<h1>Unselect All</h1>
<hr align="left" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu &gt; Unselect All</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Unselect All</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command unselects marked entities/groups that are selected (or partially selected). See</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="../User_Interface/Tree_Context_Menus.htm">Tree Context Menus</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">for details about marking tree items. This command is grayed if the entity is not selected (whole or partially) or the group does not contain selected entities. If applied to a group that contains selected as well as unselected entities, all selected entities (or their selected parts) will be unselected. It is not possible to unselect hidden entities. If you apply Unselect to the root, all objects in the scene will be unselected.</span></p>
